# Intent: the unit gets itself out of a freeze, and can never reboot-loop (owner approval 2026-11-13, "implement everything we discussed and planned"; design note docs/dev/stackchan-self-healing-2026-11-13.md, rung (b) and guard (f)). Host log 2026-11-12 23:40: tool calls timed out for three minutes while others still answered, and nothing restarted it, for two reasons the host fix (a 120 s sliding window) alone cannot cure. (1) The "system reboot" command was run through Schedule(), on the main loop, so a stuck main loop could never run it: it now runs off the receiving task, through the guard, after 300 ms so the log line and the host's ack leave first. (2) The stall watch (patch 069) only recorded a stalled main loop and, since patch 074, never restarted: after 30 s of no clock tick (the 8 s record stays as the early warning) it now asks for a self-restart. This reverses the owner's 2026-10-23 "no reboot on every stall", which was about the 10 s OpenAudioChannel wait patch 075 removed; a 30 s stall today is a real freeze. THE GUARD (main/hal/heal_guard.cpp): every self-chosen restart (host request, 30 s stall, a deaf wake engine after patch 086's rebuild) goes through maipai_heal_restart, at most 3 an hour counted in NVS (heal_n the count, heal_s the window clock in the unit's running seconds, since no clock survives a restart); the fourth is refused, logged, reported as a "heal" event (action=refused) and as heal_hold=1 in the boot and wake_stats events until the hour ends. The restart runs on its own task with an internal 4 KB stack (a flash write from the motion sensor task, whose stack is in PSRAM, aborts the unit: patch 074). Panics are not chosen, never counted here and never held back (crash_resets counts them). The boot event gains heal_n, heal_hold and heal_why (host, stall or deaf: why the last restart was chosen, empty after a power-on or a panic); wake_stats gains heal_n and heal_hold; a restart or refusal sends a "heal" event with action, why and n.
# Upstream: m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/hal_imu.cpp, hal_head_touch.cpp, device_events.h, xiaozhi-esp32/main/application.cc (MIT); main/hal/heal_guard.cpp is new (the CMake glob picks it up). Applies after 084 with --unidiff-zero.
# Check after a flash: "unit heal: heal action=restart why=host n=1" then a boot with "heal_why=host heal_n=1"; the fourth request within an hour logs "restart refused" and wake_stats says heal_hold=1; a main loop held for 30 s (not reachable on demand) logs "main loop stalled for 30 s: asking for a self-restart" and the next boot says heal_why=stall; a normal boot says heal_n=0 heal_hold=0 heal_why=.
